  "summary": "Four supplied studies directly apply representation learning with paired positive and negative examples (contrastive learning) to predicting road traffic flow: [V0237], [V0238], [V0239], and [V0240]. These four are equally direct matches and are ranked before all other candidates. Because they use different datasets and metrics, their scores should not be interpreted as a normalized head-to-head comparison. [V0237] reports 0.93 accuracy on MetroFlow; [V0238] reports MAE 0.65 on Atlas-ICU; [V0239] reports AUROC 0.72 on AgriSat-4; and [V0240] reports F1 0.79 on LedgerGuard. Only four candidates satisfy both the requested method and topic. [V0221] is listed fifth solely to meet the required five-ID output format and is not direct evidence for contrastive learning: it applies self-attention encoder models to road traffic flow on MetroFlow and reports 0.84 accuracy, making it a non-contrastive traffic comparator.",
